  "verbalization": "Methyl alpha-galactoside is implicated in the biological pathway leading to SNU-C4 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Methyl alpha-galactoside acts as a target for Hexokinase and Cytochrome c', both of which are subsequently targeted by 6-O-(3-Methoxy-4-hydroxy-trans-cinnamoyl)-beta-D-glucopyranose. This compound, in turn, is shown to have a target of SNU-C4. The integration of these pathways implies that Methyl alpha-galactoside may influence SNU-C4 through the activation of these enzymes, potentially via a metabolic or signaling cascade. The presence of multiple intermediates in the pathway, including the enzyme Hexokinase and the protein Cytochrome c', suggests a possible role in cellular metabolism or signaling, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a direct or indirect link between Methyl alpha-galactoside and SNU-C4, highlighting the importance of these intermediates in the biological process.",
